From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:06:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] um: keep no signal-stack array for Darwin carriers

A Darwin carrier takes its signal stack from the host: set_sigstack()
allocates SIGSTKSZ (128 KiB) and ignores the address and size it is
given, and stack_protections() on the array only restates a protection
the kernel image's .bss already has. cpu_irqstacks[NR_CPUS][THREAD_SIZE]
was therefore reserved and never used, NR_CPUS x THREAD_SIZE of image,
8 MiB at 128 KiB task stacks and 4 MiB at 64 KiB ones, taken from the
guest's RAM whatever its CPU count.

Define the array and protect it only where the host stack really lives
in it. The signal stacks stay 128 KiB whatever the task stacks are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/um/include/linux/smp-internal.h | 2 ++
 arch/um/kernel/skas/process.c        | 4 +++-
 arch/um/kernel/smp.c                 | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/um/include/linux/smp-internal.h b/arch/um/include/linux/smp-internal.h
index 1dbcbc23f9c90c30a22219a35e8031da3dd5a3fb..b6d2f943fce02c68d42f53984dfba722858de832 100644
--- a/arch/um/include/linux/smp-internal.h
+++ b/arch/um/include/linux/smp-internal.h
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ static inline void prefill_possible_map(void) { }
 
 #endif /* CONFIG_SMP */
 
+#ifndef UML_HOST_DARWIN
 extern char cpu_irqstacks[NR_CPUS][THREAD_SIZE] __aligned(THREAD_SIZE);
+#endif
 
 #endif /* __UM_SMP_INTERNAL_H */
diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/skas/process.c b/arch/um/kernel/skas/process.c
index e7a6d0e0fb9c2a6d3632579052ac6e69a98b9475..705b9ca9d065199f8c0e288e93eccbccf50dd8d2 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/skas/process.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/skas/process.c
@@ -29,12 +29,14 @@ static int __init start_kernel_proc(void *unused)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#ifndef UML_HOST_DARWIN
 char cpu_irqstacks[NR_CPUS][THREAD_SIZE] __aligned(THREAD_SIZE);
+#endif
 
 int __init __no_stack_protector start_uml(void)
 {
-	stack_protections((unsigned long) &cpu_irqstacks[0]);
 #ifndef UML_HOST_DARWIN
+	stack_protections((unsigned long) &cpu_irqstacks[0]);
 	set_sigstack(cpu_irqstacks[0], THREAD_SIZE);
 #endif
 
diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/smp.c b/arch/um/kernel/smp.c
index afbd7c2728430ab2119ba07251b8a7b6838877a6..b00efb7aa817c07900c2f869be746c973d8ead2a 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/smp.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/smp.c
@@ -275,8 +275,14 @@ void uml_start_secondary(void *opaque)
 	struct mm_struct *mm = &init_mm;
 	struct task_struct *idle;
 
+#ifdef UML_HOST_DARWIN
+	/* The carrier takes its signal stack from the host, not from the
+	 * kernel image. */
+	set_sigstack(NULL, 0);
+#else
 	stack_protections((unsigned long) &cpu_irqstacks[cpu]);
 	set_sigstack(&cpu_irqstacks[cpu], THREAD_SIZE);
+#endif
 
 	set_cpu_present(cpu, true);
 	os_futex_wait(&cpu_states[cpu], UML_CPU_PAUSED);
